IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`

§ `Chapter 2 -- General explanations`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 23, 24, 25, 26, 26B, 26C, 26D.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 23 -- Wrongful gain and wrongful loss`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 23(1)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a wrongful gain` IF
        f's `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another`
    AND f's `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 23(2)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a wrongful loss` IF
        f's `intends to cause wrongful loss to another`
    AND f's `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled`

§§ `Section 24 -- Dishonestly`

-- s 24(a): intention of causing wrongful gain or wrongful loss, temporary or permanent.
-- s 24(b): dishonest by ordinary standards AND A knows that.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 24"
@export Decide whether the actor does the act dishonestly under Penal Code 1871 section 24
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements of the proposed act. Set intends to cause wrongful gain / wrongful loss and the entitlement flags for s 24(a), or both ordinary-standards flags for s 24(b).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done dishonestly` IF
        `there is a wrongful gain` f
    OR  `there is a wrongful loss` f
    OR  (    f's `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons`
         AND f's `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards`)

§§ `Section 25 -- Fraudulently`

-- Intent to deceive B and by that deception an advantage accrue or detriment befall,
-- unless so slight that no reasonable person of ordinary sense or temper would complain.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 25"
@export Decide whether the actor does the act fraudulently under Penal Code 1871 section 25
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Set intends to deceive, intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall, and whether that advantage or detriment is too slight (Explanation 1).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done fraudulently` IF
        f's `intends to deceive another person`
    AND f's `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception`
    AND NOT f's `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain`

§§ `Section 26 -- Reason to believe`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor has reason to believe` IF
    f's `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance`

§§ `Section 26B -- Good faith`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26B"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done in good faith` IF
    NOT f's `is done or believed without due care and attention`

§§ `Section 26C -- Intentionally`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26C(1)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done intentionally` IF
    f's `does the act deliberately`

§§ `Section 26D -- Knowingly`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26D(1)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done knowingly` IF
        f's `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist`
    OR  `the act is done intentionally` f

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Illustrations`

`s24 gain` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS TRUE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS TRUE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS FALSE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS FALSE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS TRUE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE

`s24 standards` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS TRUE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS TRUE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS FALSE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS FALSE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS TRUE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE

`s25 slight` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS TRUE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS TRUE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS TRUE
    `does the act deliberately` IS TRUE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE

`s25 fraud` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS TRUE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS TRUE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS TRUE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the act is done dishonestly` `s24 gain`
#ASSERT `the act is done dishonestly` `s24 standards`
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is done fraudulently` `s25 slight`)
#ASSERT `the act is done fraudulently` `s25 fraud`
